## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates expertise in designing schema evolution and tenant isolation in Azure data pipelines while balancing flexibility with data integrity.

## Key Concepts

- Schema evolution and backward compatibility
- Per-tenant isolation in Delta Lake on ADLS Gen2
- Lightweight schema registry design
- Data quality gates and validation strategies
- Migration and rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: validate and route incoming record by tenant/version
async function processRecord(record, tenantId) {
  const schema = await getSchema(tenantId);
  const validationResult = validateAgainstSchema(record, schema);
  if (!validationResult.valid) {
    await sendToDeadLetterQueue(record, validationResult.errors);
    return;
  }
  await writeToDeltaLake(record, tenantId, schema.version);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle breaking changes across tenants?
- What monitoring alerts would indicate schema drift or validation failures?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design an EU-resident analytics flow with data governance, simple serverless components, and cost awareness.

## Key Concepts
- EU residency and data sovereignty
- Event-driven ingestion with Azure Event Hubs
- Serverless processing with Azure Functions
- Per-tenant access control via Cosmos DB RLS
- BYOK using Azure Key Vault
- Data retention and purge workflows
- DR planning and cost optimization

## Code Example
```javascript
module.exports = async function (context, eventHubMessages) {
  const { CosmosClient } = require('@azure/cosmos');
  const client = new CosmosClient(process.env.COSMOS_CONNECTION);
  const container = client.database('Analytics').container('TenantStats');
  for (const msg of eventHubMessages) {
    const payload = JSON.parse(msg.body);
    const item = {
      id: payload.id,
      tenantId: payload.tenantId,
      metric: payload.metric,
      value: payload.value,
      ts: new Date().toISOString()
    };
    await container.items.upsert(item);
  }
};
```

